---
import ShowcaseLayout from '../../layouts/ShowcaseLayout.astro';
import AstroPaletteDemo from '../../components/showcase/AstroPaletteDemo.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const projects = await getCollection('projects');
const project = projects.find(p => p.data.slug === 'astro-palette');

if (!project) {
  return Astro.redirect('/404');
}
---

<ShowcaseLayout project={project} lang="en">
  <div class="space-y-12">
    <section>
      <h2 id="overview">Engine Overview</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>Astro Palette</strong> engine is a mathematical bridge between astronomy and design. 
        Instead of picking random colors, it uses the positions of celestial bodies to derive a 
        harmonious OKLCH color palette that evolves in real-time.
      </p>
      <p>
        It implements a simplified version of Meeus' astronomical algorithms to calculate 
        the ecliptic longitude of planets, which then maps to the hue of the current planetary hour.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="interactive">Interactive Playground</h2>
      <p>
        Experiment with the engine below. Change the date, your location, or the calculation 
        mode to see how the palette shifts. The <strong>Geocentric</strong> mode produces a 
        unique palette every day, while <strong>Fixed</strong> follows a weekly planetary cycle.
      </p>
      <AstroPaletteDemo />
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="logic">The Logic</h2>
      <p>
        The palette is built on three pillars:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Planetary Hours:</strong> Based on the Chaldean order, determining the "Ruler" of the current hour.</li>
        <li><strong>OKLCH Space:</strong> Ensures perceptual uniformity, meaning the "brightness" and "intensity" of colors stay consistent even as the hue changes.</li>
        <li><strong>Aspect Modulation:</strong> (Optional) Boosts chroma or lightness when planets form specific geometric aspects (like conjunctions or oppositions).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</ShowcaseLayout>
